       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB184GVA.
      *> ISO 13.18.63.4 GR5 - "If a VALUE clause is specified in a data
      *> description entry of a group item, the group AREA is
      *> initialized without consideration for the individual
      *> elementary or group items contained within this group."  THE
      *> LITERAL'S CHARACTERS ARE DEPOSITED POSITIONALLY ACROSS THE
      *> GROUP'S STORAGE AND EACH SUBORDINATE IS THEN WHATEVER ITS OWN
      *> DESCRIPTION MAKES OF THE CHARACTERS UNDER IT.  GR7 ALIGNS THE
      *> LITERAL PER 14.6.8 (LEFT-JUSTIFIED, SPACE FILL, NO EDITING).
      *>
      *> THIS IS THE CONFORMING HALF OF kb/Work PB184.  ITS NOTE
      *> MEASURED `01 GV VALUE "40537". 05 GB PIC 9 COMP-5 OCCURS 5.`
      *> LEAVING EVERY OCCURRENCE ZERO AND READ THAT AS A GR5
      *> DISTRIBUTION GAP OVER BYTE-FORM LEAVES.  13.18.63.3 SR14
      *> REFUTES THE PREMISE - A COMP-5 LEAF UNDER AN ALPHANUMERIC
      *> GROUP ITEM CARRYING A VALUE IS NOT USAGE DISPLAY, SO THAT
      *> PROGRAM IS NOT CONFORMING (COBOLNET1702, THE THREE
      *> pb184-group-value-* NEGATIVE FIXTURES).  WHAT GR5 GOVERNS IS
      *> THE POPULATION SR14 ADMITS, WHERE EVERY SUBORDINATE IS USAGE
      *> DISPLAY AND THE CHARACTER IMAGE IS THE BYTE IMAGE - AND THAT
      *> IS WHAT THIS PROGRAM PINS, IN BOTH INITIALIZER LANES.
      *>
      *> LANE 1 (S*) - THE TYPED-NATIVE RECORD-STRUCT LANE: NO ALIAS,
      *>   SO GroupValueSlicer DISTRIBUTES THE AREA INTO THE FIELDS.
      *> LANE 2 (C*) - THE CHARACTER-IMAGE LANE: THE REDEFINES MAKES
      *>   THE GROUP A TIER-B CLASS WHOSE BACKING IS SEEDED BY
      *>   GroupImageCodec.ImageInitOf - THE ONE SEEDER SINCE PB164 FOR
      *>   EVERY TIER-B / EXTERNAL / BASED / OO BACKING.  THAT SEEDER
      *>   WALKED STRAIGHT PAST THE GROUP'S OWN VALUE INTO THE MEMBERS,
      *>   SO C4 MEASURED [  ][  ][    ] ON 8ca74a3d WHILE ITS
      *>   UNALIASED TWIN GAVE [AB][CD] - THE WHOLE VALUE LOST TO
      *>   NOTHING BUT THE PRESENCE OF AN ALIAS.  13.18.63.3 SR12 BARS
      *>   A VALUE IN THE REDEFINING ENTRY, NEVER IN THE REDEFINED ONE,
      *>   SO CT IS CONFORMING SOURCE.  READ AT BYTE LEVEL THROUGH THE
      *>   X VIEW WITH FUNCTION ORD (15.70), NEVER A SELF-INVERSE ROUND
      *>   TRIP, SO THE CLAIM IS ABOUT STORAGE AND NOT A RENDERING.
      *>
      *> THE FIGURATIVE ARM (SZ/SQ/CZ) WAS THE THIRD DEFECT THE SWEEP
      *> FOUND: SR13 ADMITS "a figurative constant that is permitted in
      *> a MOVE statement to a receiving item of that category", AND
      *> 8.3.3.6.4 GR2 MAKES IT ONE CHARACTER REPEATED TO THE
      *> RECEIVER'S SIZE - SO SZ IS FOUR '0' CHARACTERS.  IT MEASURED
      *> FOUR SPACES: THE AREA RULE HANDLED QUOTED AND ALL-LITERAL
      *> OPERANDS AND DROPPED FIGURATIVE WORDS TO THE MEMBER-WISE
      *> DEFAULT.  ALL THREE FORMS NOW COME FROM ONE RULE
      *> (GroupValueSlicer.AreaTextOf), RIDDEN BY BOTH LANES.
      *> GR2 IS THE RULE FOR ALL THREE OPERAND FORMS BECAUSE IT IS THE
      *> BRANCH FOR "the length of the string is specified in the rules
      *> for the context", IT NAMES THE VALUE CLAUSE, AND IT CARRIES
      *> BOTH THE REPEAT AND THE TRUNCATE-FROM-THE-RIGHT.  GR3 IS THE
      *> COMPLEMENTARY BRANCH - THE LENGTH *NOT* SPECIFIED - AND ITS
      *> SUB-RULE a IS SCOPED TO A CONCATENATION EXPRESSION; NEITHER
      *> GOVERNS HERE, SINCE 13.18.63.4 GR5 MAKES THE GROUP AREA THE
      *> RECEIVING FIELD AND SO SPECIFIES THE LENGTH.  THE FILL
      *> CHARACTER ITSELF IS GR1'S, WITH THE PER-FORMAT GR4-GR8
      *> IDENTITIES ('0', SPACE, '"').
      *>
      *> S5 / CL / CQ CLOSE THE OPERAND-FORM x LANE MATRIX: THE `ALL
      *>   <figurative-word>` SPELLING WAS PINNED BY NEITHER LANE, AND
      *>   `ALL "literal"` ONLY BY THE SLICER (SL).
      *> TV IS THE POSITIVE CONTROL FOR THE SCREEN'S WIDENED SUBJECT
      *>   SET.  13.18.57.4 GR3 MAKES A REFERENCE-SITE VALUE THE INITIAL
      *>   VALUE OF THE SUBJECT, AND COBOLNET1702 NOW WALKS THE COMPOSED
      *>   FOREST TO SEE IT (negative/pb184-group-value-type-reference).
      *>   AN ALL-DISPLAY TEMPLATE IS THE LEGAL HALF: SR14 IS SATISFIED,
      *>   SO GR5 MUST DEPOSIT THE AREA ACROSS THE CLONED MEMBERS AND
      *>   THE SCREEN MUST STAY SILENT.  A WIDENED SCREEN THAT ALSO
      *>   OVER-REJECTED WOULD PASS EVERY NEGATIVE FIXTURE.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 SA VALUE "40537".
          05 SDX PIC 9 OCCURS 5.
       01 SZ VALUE ZEROS.
          05 SZ1 PIC X(2).
          05 SZ2 PIC X(2).
       01 SQ VALUE QUOTES.
          05 SQ1 PIC X(4).
       01 SL VALUE ALL "-".
          05 SL1 PIC X(2).
          05 SL2 PIC X(2).
       01 S5 VALUE ALL ZEROS.
          05 S51 PIC X(2).
          05 S52 PIC X(2).
       01 TD IS TYPEDEF.
          05 TD1 PIC X(2).
          05 TD2 PIC X(2).
       01 TV TYPE TD VALUE "WXYZ".
       01 CA VALUE "40537".
          05 CDX PIC 9 OCCURS 5.
       01 RA REDEFINES CA PIC X(5).
       01 CZ VALUE ZEROS.
          05 CZ1 PIC X(2).
          05 CZ2 PIC X(2).
       01 RZ REDEFINES CZ PIC X(4).
       01 CT VALUE "ABCD".
          05 CT1 PIC X(2).
          05 CT2 PIC X(2).
       01 RT REDEFINES CT PIC X(4).
      *> A SHORT LITERAL: GR7 / 14.6.8 SPACE-FILLS THE REST OF THE
      *> AREA, IT DOES NOT LEAVE THE TAIL MEMBER AT ITS OWN DEFAULT.
       01 CS VALUE "AB".
          05 CS1 PIC X(2).
          05 CS2 PIC X(2).
       01 RS REDEFINES CS PIC X(4).
       01 CL VALUE ALL "-".
          05 CL1 PIC X(2).
          05 CL2 PIC X(2).
       01 RL REDEFINES CL PIC X(4).
       01 CQ VALUE ALL ZEROS.
          05 CQ1 PIC X(2).
          05 CQ2 PIC X(2).
       01 RQ REDEFINES CQ PIC X(4).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           DISPLAY "S1=" SDX(1) SDX(2) SDX(3) SDX(4) SDX(5)
           DISPLAY "S2=[" SZ1 "][" SZ2 "]"
           DISPLAY "S3=[" SQ1 "]"
           DISPLAY "S4=[" SL1 "][" SL2 "]"
           DISPLAY "C1=" CDX(1) CDX(2) CDX(3) CDX(4) CDX(5)
           DISPLAY "C2=" FUNCTION ORD(RA(1:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RA(2:1))
               " " FUNCTION ORD(RA(3:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RA(4:1))
               " " FUNCTION ORD(RA(5:1))
           DISPLAY "C3=[" CZ1 "][" CZ2 "][" RZ "]"
           DISPLAY "C4=[" CT1 "][" CT2 "][" RT "]"
           DISPLAY "C5=" FUNCTION ORD(RT(1:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(RT(4:1))
           DISPLAY "C6=[" CS1 "][" CS2 "][" RS "]"
           DISPLAY "S5=[" S51 "][" S52 "]"
           DISPLAY "C7=[" CL1 "][" CL2 "][" RL "]"
           DISPLAY "C8=[" CQ1 "][" CQ2 "][" RQ "]"
           DISPLAY "TV=[" TD1 OF TV "][" TD2 OF TV "]"
           STOP RUN.
